# Microfinance Management System - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Daily Collection Management System (DCMS) for a microfinance company. It manages daily collections, client accounts, agent operations, loan processing, and financial reporting with strict security and compliance requirements.

## Core Principles

### 1. Security First
- NEVER store sensitive data (passwords, PINs, account numbers) in plain text
- Always use encryption for data at rest and in transit
- Implement proper authentication and authorization for all endpoints
- Follow the principle of least privilege for all user roles
- Implement audit logging for ALL financial transactions
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Validate and sanitize ALL user inputs
- Implement rate limiting on authentication endpoints
- Use secure session management with proper timeouts
- Never expose sensitive information in error messages or logs

### 2. Financial Compliance
- All monetary values must use DECIMAL types (never FLOAT or DOUBLE)
- Implement double-entry bookkeeping principles
- Every transaction must be atomic (ACID properties)
- Implement idempotency for all financial operations
- Maintain complete audit trails with timestamps and user identification
- Implement the four-eye principle (dual authorization) for critical operations
- All amounts must be validated before processing
- Implement transaction rollback mechanisms
- Use database transactions for all financial operations
- Never allow negative balances unless explicitly authorized (loan scenarios)

### 3. Data Integrity
- Use database constraints for data validation
- Implement soft deletes (never hard delete financial records)
- Maintain historical records of all changes
- Implement versioning for critical entities
- Use checksums or hash verification for transaction integrity
- Implement data backup and recovery mechanisms
- Validate all foreign key relationships
- Use appropriate data types for all fields

