## Architecture Patterns

### 1. Layered Architecture
```
├── Presentation Layer (Controllers/Routes)
├── Business Logic Layer (Services)
├── Data Access Layer (Repositories)
└── Database Layer
```

### 2. Authentication & Authorization
- Implement JWT or session-based authentication
- Use bcrypt or Argon2 for password hashing (minimum cost factor: 12)
- Implement role-based access control (RBAC):
  - Administrator: Full system access
  - Accountant: Financial operations, client management
  - Agent: Limited to assigned collection areas
  - Client: Read-only access to own account
- Implement permission-based authorization for granular control
- Use refresh tokens for extended sessions
- Implement account lockout after failed login attempts (e.g., 5 attempts)
- Require strong passwords (minimum 8 characters, mix of uppercase, lowercase, numbers, symbols)

### 3. Transaction Management Pattern
```typescript
// Example pattern for financial transactions
async function executeTransaction(transactionData) {
  const dbTransaction = await db.beginTransaction();
  try {
    // 1. Validate transaction
    await validateTransaction(transactionData);
    
    // 2. Check balances and limits
    await checkBusinessRules(transactionData);
    
    // 3. Create audit log entry (pending)
    const auditId = await createAuditLog(transactionData, 'PENDING');
    
    // 4. Execute the transaction
    const result = await performTransaction(transactionData, dbTransaction);
    
    // 5. Update audit log (completed)
    await updateAuditLog(auditId, 'COMPLETED', result);
    
    // 6. Commit transaction
    await dbTransaction.commit();
    
    return result;
  } catch (error) {
    // Rollback on any error
    await dbTransaction.rollback();
    await updateAuditLog(auditId, 'FAILED', error);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

