## Four-Eye Principle Implementation

### Transaction Approval Workflow
1. Agent/Accountant initiates transaction
2. Transaction saved with status: PENDING_APPROVAL
3. Notification sent to Administrator
4. Administrator reviews transaction details
5. Administrator approves or rejects
6. If approved: status changes to COMPLETED
7. If rejected: status changes to REJECTED with reason
8. Audit log records all actions

### Implementation Example
```javascript
// Transaction approval system
const transactionStates = {
  DRAFT: 'DRAFT',
  PENDING_APPROVAL: 'PENDING_APPROVAL',
  APPROVED: 'APPROVED',
  REJECTED: 'REJECTED',
  COMPLETED: 'COMPLETED'
};

// Only administrator can approve
async function approveTransaction(transactionId, approverId) {
  // Verify approver is administrator
  const approver = await getUser(approverId);
  if (approver.role !== 'ADMINISTRATOR') {
    throw new UnauthorizedError('Only administrators can approve transactions');
  }
  
  // Update transaction status
  await updateTransaction(transactionId, {
    status: transactionStates.APPROVED,
    approvedBy: approverId,
    approvedAt: new Date()
  });
}
```

## Daily Operations Flow

### System Startup
1. System starts when server is powered on
2. Initialize database connections
3. Load system configuration
4. Start audit logging
5. Enable user authentication

### Daily Collection Process
1. Agent collects cash from clients
2. Agent logs into system
3. Agent enters collected amounts (Ventilation)
4. System validates entries
5. Transactions marked as PENDING_APPROVAL
6. Administrator reviews and approves at end of day
7. System updates account balances
8. Generate daily collection report

### Day Closure
1. Administrator reviews all pending transactions
2. Administrator approves/rejects transactions
3. System calculates daily totals
4. System checks for surpluses/shortages
5. Generate end-of-day reports
6. Close accounting day (no further transactions allowed)
7. Backup database

